            view: 'The business underneath the noise is better than the stock suggests, and the Committee should know what it is declining. **Excipients are 1-2% of a formulation\'s cost but can ruin a batch, so formulators are extremely reluctant to requalify** — and Sigachi is proving it has that pricing power, with MCC realisations up from ₹216 to ₹241/kg driving sequential margin improvement on flat volumes. Two genuine mix upgrades sit behind it: an 1,800 tonne croscarmellose plant shifting revenue toward disintegrants realising **₹1,200-1,500/kg, five to six times bulk MCC**, and an API division pivoting to regulated markets with its own research centre, already scaling Sparsentan and Bempedoic acid. On a clean balance sheet this would be an interesting small-cap.',
            watch: '**The governance stack is the reason to pass. Legal proceedings against the MD and CEO following the Hyderabad fire; roughly 26% of promoter holding pledged with invocations already reducing the stake; Dahej delayed a full year to FY28; a delayed insurance payout management concedes will be haircut; and an openly acknowledged possibility of a preferential raise against a ₹250cr-plus capex bill.** The return on capital has fallen to 6.14%, FY27 guidance of ₹650-675cr is mathematically strained against the current run rate at capped capacity, and clients forced onto secondary vendors during the shutdown have not all come back.',
