            what: 'Business-to-business micronutrient premixes, ready-to-use therapeutic foods for institutional buyers, and a nascent consumer brand.',
            view: 'A profitable, genuinely niche position at an undemanding 19.6x. **The premix moat is technical: vitamins and minerals interact unpredictably in processing, and guaranteeing formulation stability is what embeds Hexagon in customers\' supply chains** — a food or pharma company does not re-tender a premix it has validated. Therapeutic foods add regulatory capture through international NGO standards. FY26 delivered 17.8% growth with EBITDA up 32%, and management guides 20-25% forward.',
            watch: 'Newly listed, so governance and use of IPO proceeds are untested — worth four to six quarters of observation. Therapeutic foods depend on lumpy NGO and government funding cycles, and moving into consumer nutrition invites customer-acquisition costs into a 13.8% margin structure. Watch marketing spend as a share of revenue.',
